Using the Carrier psychrometric equation, with \(p_{ws}(65^\circ\mathrm F)\approx0.3057\) psia:

\[
p_v=p_{ws}-\frac{(P-p_{ws})(T_{DB}-T_{WB})}{2800-1.3T_{WB}}
\]

\[
p_v=0.3057-\frac{(14.7-0.3057)(85-65)}{2800-1.3(65)}
\approx0.1997\ \text{psia}
\]

Thus the specific humidity is

\[
W=0.622\frac{p_v}{P-p_v}
=0.622\frac{0.1997}{14.7-0.1997}
\approx0.00857\ \frac{\text{lb water}}{\text{lb dry air}}
\]

Using \(p_{ws}(85^\circ\mathrm F)\approx0.596\) psia:

\[
\phi=\frac{p_v}{p_{ws}(85^\circ\mathrm F)}
\approx\frac{0.1997}{0.596}\approx33.5\%
\]

The dew point is the temperature at which the saturation pressure equals \(0.1997\) psia, approximately \(53.1^\circ\mathrm F\). These values match **option C**.

Response A’s psychrometric calculation is incorrect, and its final choice H does not even agree with its own intermediate results. Response B’s answer C is correct.

