For a harmonic diatomic oscillator,

\[
\tilde{\nu}=\frac{1}{2\pi c}\sqrt{\frac{k}{\mu}},
\qquad
\mu=\frac{35\,\mathrm{u}}{2}
=2.9059\times10^{-26}\ \mathrm{kg}.
\]

Thus,

\[
\sqrt{\frac{k}{\mu}}
=\sqrt{\frac{319}{2.9059\times10^{-26}}}
=\sqrt{1.0978\times10^{28}}
=1.0478\times10^{14}\ \mathrm{s^{-1}},
\]

and therefore

\[
\tilde{\nu}
=\frac{1.0478\times10^{14}}
{2\pi(2.9979\times10^{10})}
\approx 556\ \mathrm{cm^{-1}}.
\]

The correct choice is **(F)**. Response B made a square-root arithmetic error, leading to its incorrect result and final answer.

