The spacing \(d=2.665\times10^{-8}\ \text{cm}\) is the nearest-neighbor K–F distance. For the rock-salt structure, the conventional cubic cell has edge length \(a=2d=5.33\times10^{-8}\ \text{cm}\) and contains \(Z=4\) KF formula units.

Using \(M_{\mathrm{KF}}=58.1\ \text{g/mol}\):

\[
N_A=\frac{ZM}{\rho a^3}
=\frac{4(58.1)}
{2.48(5.33\times10^{-8})^3}
\approx 6.19\times10^{23}\ \text{mol}^{-1}.
\]

Thus the correct choice is **(I) \(6.2\times10^{23}\)**. Response A incorrectly used \(d\) as the full unit-cell edge while retaining four formula units per cell, so its answer (E) is wrong.

